      "content": "that's a good start. but i'm worried some critics might find the comparison a bit too balanced. when we talk about 'artistic merit' in a museum setting, usually the technical mastery of things like perspective and anatomy is given more weight in terms of pure aesthetic achievement. \n\ndo you think it's fair to say that the Renaissance work represents a higher level of individual artistic genius, whereas the African pieces are more about collective tradition and repetition of patterns rather than individual innovation? i want to make sure the catalog reflects the difference in their technical sophistication.",
